// DISABLE_NATIVE: targetFamily=MINGW


// KT-54330 window, sibling of the corpus case inline/privateClassDefaultCtorStubLinkage:
// the private class is never constructed. It is reachable from main (a friend module) only
// through an `is` check inside a private inline body, which the internal inline g inlines.
//
// main's inlined code evaluates `x is Hidden`, so its per-file object references the private
// class Hidden's `kclass:` typeinfo global as an external symbol. But
// CacheInfoBuilder.trackCallees (CacheInfoBuilder.kt) walks the exported inline bodies with
// a visitor that handles only calls, constructor calls, object singletons, enum getters and
// function/property references - it has no visitor for IrTypeOperatorCall (or IrGetClass,
// or IrCatch), and it sets isConstructedFromExportedInlineFunctions only from constructor
// calls. Hidden is therefore never marked, and LlvmDeclarations.createClassDeclarations
// (LlvmDeclarations.kt) emits Hidden's typeinfo+vtable global with LLVM internal linkage
// in lib1's per-file object (external only when the class is exported, or
// producePerFileCache && isConstructedFromExportedInlineFunctions - the KT-54330 fix,
// which this gap bypasses). Internal definition in lib1's object + undefined extern
// reference in main's object = undefined symbol at the IC link. Without per-file caches
// everything is one LLVM module, the internal symbol resolves, and the program answers
// false.
//
// The same campaign reduced two more windows of the same gap with distinct fix surfaces:
// a REIFIED type argument (checkC -> probeC -> isT<C>: call type arguments are IrTypes,
// invisible to acceptChildrenVoid, so a body-scanning fix would miss it) and a CATCH
// clause filter (IrToBitcode's CatchScope.genHandler emits genInstanceOfImpl on the catch
// parameter type; trackCallees has no IrCatch visitor). See
// r2t5-r2-reified-private-class-typeinf/reduce/manual and
// r3t6-r3t6-catch-clause-typeinfo/reduce/manual under this campaign's output.
//
// Harness note: the "clean" reference link also enables incremental compilation (with a
// fresh cache), so this from-scratch IC-only defect fails both of the harness's links and
// the run is reported as INVALID. The bug is the IC-only link failure: the same klibs link
// and answer false without -Xenable-incremental-compilation.

MODULES: lib1, main

STEP 0:
    libs: lib1, main
